The attached image, Figure 5 from the Journal of Controlled Release (2015) paper, demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, displaying flow cytometry dot plots, shows that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) or Nano-11 alone results in moderate cellular uptake, co-incubation with Nano-11+OVA leads to a substantial increase in cells positive for both, indicating efficient co-delivery. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, further confirms this by showing a significant shift towards higher OVA uptake when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11 compared to OVA or Nano-11 alone, highlighting Nano-11's role in facilitating antigen presentation.